WEBVTT

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.440
Hey, those men are back again.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.650
Well, if you think about it, 
Aoyama is a national age-group player.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.970
It's not surprising they'd
 show up to scout him.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.410
That means there's no guarantee 
he'll be with us to the end.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.220
<i>Aoyama might leave...</i>

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.750
Zaizen. Hey, Zaizen.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:37.260
Our days of dreaming about reaching 
Nationals might be numbered.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.580
He only came here because 
he liked the toilets.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.730
If he's going to a pro youth club,
he'll have no reason to remain with us.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:54.030
<b>#12</b>

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:54.030
<b>The Reason Behind Aoyama-kun's Choice</b>

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.980
Hey, Aoyama!

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.690
We need to talk.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:03.830
Are you going to join a youth club?

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.530
Those scouts were here again.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:14.010
I don't want to be blunt, 
but everybody's relying on you.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.460
You're our team's—

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.090
Look! It's Aoyama-san, 
the youth national player!

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:20.850
Seriously?

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.250
It's true! Oh, my god!

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.060
I always keep an eye out for your matches!

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.180
Can we get your autograph?

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.070
<i>You're our team's...</i>

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.550
<i>...biggest hope.</i>

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:40.050
Wow, even his autograph is amazing!

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.100
I'm going to treasure this forever!

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:43.910
<i>Just kidding.</i>

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.540
We actually got one!

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:46.170
Aoyama!

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.590
Yeah!

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:47.810
So lucky!

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:52.590
You should play where 
you can shine the most.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.840
But...

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.260
Let's do our best tomorrow.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.630
Mother!

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.290
What is it?

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.490
Please come to my next soccer match.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.660
I'm going to score a goal
for you as a present!

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.040
Let's get going.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.460
Yes, Daddy.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.030
You have your match now, don't you?

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:41.630
Yes.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.930
<i>Mother, I promise that 
we will win today's match!</i>

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:55.440
<b>Inter-High
Tokyo City
First Preliminaries</b>

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.930
"You eleven knights who are 
gathered on this holy ground..."

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:03.370
<b>Thanks to its 
ongoing popularity, 
Season 2 of the 
anime is greenlit!</b>

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:01.620
"I am going to join the battle as well!"

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.370
"Let's save the world together!"

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.830
For some reason, I feel like this 
week's chapter is cheering us on!

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.290
I can feel the power!

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.390
Is Aoyama-kun really going to quit our team?

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:29.470
No clue! I have no idea what he's thinking.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.100
Just like her...

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.520
Huh?

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.070
Oh, nothing.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.820
She's pretty.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.430
Is that your mom?

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.240
What the hell, you guys?
What is it to you?!

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.110
Don't be so shy and introduce us.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.620
Are you into older women?

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.960
That's my mother!

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:56.300
Besides, my mother's long...

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.070
Zaizen?

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.840
Listen up! Time for the pre-match meeting!

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:08.060
Let's review what we know 
about today's opponent.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.630
What do you make of Zaizen's reaction?

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:12.860
He had a pretty serious look on his face.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.520
Actually, I happened to see something 
when I was walking my dog this morning.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.990
Zaizen was paying his respects 
at a grave with his father.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.730
Wait, does that mean today's 
 the day Zaizen's mom...

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.690
...passed away?

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.030
Really?

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.450
Hey, guys!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.700
Be quiet! Anyway, moving on.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:39.110
Our opponent, Kuraishi High School, 
has two powerful center backs.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:41.820
They're a team whose rise is
built on an ironclad defense.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.020
In order to breach their defense,

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.810
we need you to shine
as brightly as you can, Kaocchi.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:57.100
Kaocchi?

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.690
Y-Yes!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.800
Pull it together, everyone. 
Let's go win another match!

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:03.900
Yes, ma'am!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.500
Captain!

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.500
Yeah!

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.090
Where's Zaizen?

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:23.540
He went to the bathroom.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:25.420
Good, because...

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.700
Today's the anniversary...

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.350
...of Zaizen's mom's death?

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:29.990
Why didn't he say something?

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:30.750
Yeah, how come?

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.890
There's only one thing we can do.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.430
Provide support for Zaizen!

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.830
We'll send everything his way...

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:37.970
...and help him score...

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.090
...to cheer him up!

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.330
Our team will win.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:41.860
And we'll advance from the preliminaries!

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.820
Sounds good. I bet his mother 
would like that, too.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:51.540
Sorry for making you all wait.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:54.710
All right!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.170
<i>That's my cue as captain!</i>

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:58.780
Fujimi—

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:00.130
Victory at any cost!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.590
Fujimi High!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.550
Fight!

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.910
All right, I'm pumped!

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.930
I can taste victory already.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:15.600
Huh? I haven't said anything yet...

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.560
There's the cross!

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.940
It looks good!

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:33.660
With your build, I bet you're 
pretty confident in the air.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.610
But quite frankly, you've got
no chance when you're facing us.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.580
<i>Bastard.</i>

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:46.030
No wonder those center backs are called
the "Double Wall of Kuraishi High."

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:49.500
They're both physically strong,
and they cover a wide range on the pitch.

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:51.260
Hm...

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:54.500
Well, I could easily obliterate them.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.380
Aoyama!

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:00.830
Their defense is quick to hound him!

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:03.230
Their anti-Aoyama strategy's good, too!

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:04.940
They have a good defense.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:08.900
He was pushed out of it again!

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.820
A long ball!

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:14.580
Oh no!

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.050
Dammit!

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.140
Gotcha!

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:26.170
They executed that counter perfectly!

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.300
So Kuraishi High School has taken the lead.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:32.380
This match is as good as ours.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:37.600
Kuraishi High School has won every 
match so far without conceding.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.820
Even scoring one goal won't be easy.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.060
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.060
<b>Kuraishi</b>

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.660
It's good that we took the lead
in the first half, but...

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.090
I would have liked to get 
another one or two goals.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.530
We need to be extra careful 
of Aoyama in the second half.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.300
Ow!

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:04.420
Kazu-kun!

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:09.380
You scraped your leg. 
We need to rinse it off.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.700
<i>She was always into something.</i>

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.740
<i>Once she caught the bug for it, 
she was blind to everything else.</i>

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:22.310
<i>Because of that, it was always Jeeves 
who took me to and from kindergarten.</i>

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.540
<i>But I was glad to just have her around.</i>

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.730
Mother! I got into the starting eleven
for the next match!

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:40.260
Jeeves, where's Mother?

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:42.860
Young Master Kaoru...

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:48.510
Your mother has gone to a faraway place.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.940
Once this match is over, Aoyama will also...

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:00.010
Dammit!

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.060
We <i>will </i>win today's match!

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:06.210
That will be my parting gift
to her and Aoyama!

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.780
<i>Congratulations! You're a winner!</i>

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:14.240
What the hell's going on?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.050
This is too much! You're broken, yo!

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:24.040
<b>Zaizen Shiori</b>

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:24.040
<b>I'm Kaoru's mother</b>

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:27.040
<b>Shoot for victory at Nationals!</b>

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:27.040
<b>Fujimi High School Eleven</b>

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.000
<i>Dwelling on it won't help!</i>

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.500
Zaizen!

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:32.460
<i>Right now, I need to focus on the game!</i>

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.060
Jeez, what are you doing?

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.050
Zaizen, back pass!

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:46.440
Crap!

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:51.740
<i>I'm counting on your aerial prowess
to get past that defensive wall!</i>

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.030
Corner to Kuraishi High School!

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:00.450
Kuraishi scores!

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.410
Crap!

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.130
That's Kuraishi High School's second goal.

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:18.300
I can't believe Aoyama-kun's
pushing forward this early in the game.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:21.730
He must be feeling the heat, too.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.260
Their closing down is almost instant!

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:27.230
Aoyama, pass it to me! That's too risky!

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.820
I guess he took one touch too many.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.070
Even for you, that was reckless!

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:38.150
What?

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:43.550
It would have been pointless to 
pass to you in your current state.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:45.350
What?

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.580
The ball!

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.540
Zaizen, the ball!

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.110
I missed?

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.140
<i>Why aren't you here...</i>

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.350
<i>...Mother?</i>

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:06.430
Zaizen!

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:10.830
Crap!

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:16.260
We've been caught upfield. Fall back!

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.260
<i>Damn, what's wrong with me?!</i>

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:22.700
Go for the counter!

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.620
<i>All right, good!</i>

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:27.340
<i>The most dangerous thing
about their team is</i>

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:31.120
<i>Aoyama's explosive offense 
in the last five minutes.</i>

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:35.000
<i>The key is how far ahead 
we are by that point.</i>

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.090
<i>We can't relax with a mere two-goal lead!</i>

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:43.970
<i>A three-goal lead will do it, though!</i>

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.390
Not on my watch!

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:48.490
<i>This is checkmate!</i>

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.300
Oh no!

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:52.930
<i>Got it!</i>

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.060
Aoyama put his body on the line to stop it!

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:20.010
Hmph, Fujimi High School barely survived.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.750
That was amazing, Aoyama!

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.090
You saved us!

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.020
Hey! Are you okay?!

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:28.940
Stay away.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:32.870
Hey, those stains...

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.300
You can't play like that.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.360
<i>It's my fault.</i>

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.770
<i>It's because I screwed up.</i>

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:42.320
Zaizen-san.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.990
If you don't want to win, 
please get yourself substituted.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:51.700
Let's do our best tomorrow.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.810
<i>Are you kidding me, Aoyama?</i>

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:04.510
I am...

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.060
...not leaving this game!

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.740
How stupid do you have to be 
to headbutt the goalpost?!

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.370
Let go of me!

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:23.070
All right, just calm down!

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.460
Is his head okay? In all senses of the word.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:31.520
Forget about the idiotic headbutter.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:36.290
What's huge is that Aoyama being 
dirty has rendered him sluggish.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.960
We have this match in the bag.

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:42.330
<i>Aoyama-kun, if you're that dirty...</i>

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:45.100
Listen up!

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:51.170
Fujimi High School is 
not just Aoyama's team.

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.630
<i>Damn that Aoyama.</i>

00:13:56.630 --> 00:14:01.230
If you don't want to win, 
please get yourself substituted.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.190
<i>I don't want to win?</i>

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:09.110
<i>Of course I want...</i>

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:12.080
<i>...to win!</i>

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.510
<i>This guy!</i>

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.960
Too bad.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.420
They took it!

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.880
Now that Aoyama's sluggish,
this is our chance!

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:25.510
A counterattack's coming!

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.790
This is the end!

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.140
How do you like that?!

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.930
He stopped their counter with his face!

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:47.110
He's got guts!

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:51.070
Looks like you got over whatever 
was bothering you, Kaocchi!

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:52.820
Ow.

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:56.430
Your soccer is so dirty.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:00.510
You moron.

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:06.300
This sort of stuff is my job.

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:09.740
Let's win this match.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:10.980
Of course.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:24.230
They keep passing the ball around 
to chip away at Fujimi's stamina.

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:31.200
This is the extent of this team's abilities
when their ace, Aoyama, isn't performing.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:35.660
There're less than ten minutes left.
They intend to let the clock run down.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.990
At this rate, Fujimi will lose.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.350
<i>Damn it all!</i>

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:45.590
<i>We need to score right now!</i>

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:48.550
<i>So I won't let them tell me
 they're at their limit!</i>

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.270
<i>My legs are like this,</i>

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:55.010
<i>and my head's fuzzy from being oxygen 
deprived because I've run around too much.</i>

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:56.970
Itou-san!

00:15:59.130 --> 00:15:59.930
<i>But you know what?</i>

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:03.900
<i>Compared to when I was moping around,</i>

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:06.380
<i>this is a lot better!</i>

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:07.860
Son of a...

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.060
Nice, Zaizen!

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:10.960
Time for us to counter!

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.820
Stop their number 5!

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:16.330
Die!

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:21.350
I won't let you stop me so easily!

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:24.250
Captain!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:25.760
Too far!

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.190
He can't make that!

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:30.830
That idiot!

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:33.110
That was our only chance!

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:35.980
Aoyama!

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:38.140
I thought he couldn't move!

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.230
It's the last five minutes!

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:50.320
I'm still on you!

00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:57.510
<i>Where are you aiming?</i>

00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:59.150
<i>There's nobody over there!</i>

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.870
Kaocchi!

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.110
<i>This ball...</i>

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.990
<i>I will make it count!</i>

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:14.290
<i>My leg!</i>

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:22.510
<i>After we've come so far?!</i>

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:23.530
Zaizen-san.

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:27.700
Zaizen!

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:28.820
Zaizen-san.

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:29.680
Zaizen!

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:30.650
Zaizen!

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:39.190
<i>Mother!</i>

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:45.710
You can do it, Kaoru!

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.850
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.850
<b>Kuraishi</b>

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:13.090
Fujimi High won again, huh?

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.500
Par for the course, no?

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:21.650
I just remembered our
 first training match.

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:25.150
Show me your leg already!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.460
It's fine. I just pulled a muscle.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:31.410
Anyway, why'd you bother showing up now?

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:35.450
Haven't we seen that person before?

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.690
Wasn't she in the picture Zaizen had?

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.780
Zaizen's mom?!

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:46.180
Yes?

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:48.690
She's fit as a fiddle!

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:52.650
Then why'd you visit the graveyard 
this morning? Talk about misleading!

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:54.150
That was to honor our ancestors.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:58.020
Dadd—I mean, Father only 
had time to go this morning.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:02.740
Give us back the energy we wasted on 
being worried about you! You idiot!

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:04.930
What are you even talking about?!

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:07.250
I'm relieved to see you having fun.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:12.520
After all this time? I don't care if you 
were volunteering or whatever!

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:14.910
Where have you been this whole time?

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:20.250
At first, I meant to come back straight away.

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:25.430
But before I knew it, it had been five years.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:28.020
You're always like this!

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:32.130
I came to see you score a goal today.

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.350
I was really watching.

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:42.870
I'm going to score a goal
for you as a present!

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:56.100
A present five years in the making.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:59.790
<i>You remembered.</i>

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.710
You're so late, Mother.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:17.190
Madam, I've come to pick you up!

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:27.120
Okay, I'm off to Brazil now.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.830
Bye!

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:34.270
Mother!

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:39.610
Mother...

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:56.670
Aoyama.

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:01.890
What are you going to do about the team?

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.860
You're joining a youth club, right?

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:06.740
I'm not, though.

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:08.010
Really?!

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:16.830
It seems you don't understand 
your own position here.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:21.420
You're already carrying the future 
of Japanese soccer on your shoulders.

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:25.300
Why is a player who's going to be 
the jewel in Japan's crown

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:29.250
not playing for a renowned school
or a youth club,

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.580
instead of here at Fujimi High School?

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:39.350
I...

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.400
...like white uniforms.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.330
The white of cleanliness!

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:52.770
Clean! Clean! A-o-ya-ma!

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.090
Aoyama-kun likes white.

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:58.830
He li-kes wh-i-te!

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:05.060
Are you kidding us?!

00:23:18.650 --> 00:23:21.180
Picking a team based on the uniform

00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:24.580
is so idiotic that I'm mad at 
myself for being worried.

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:31.850
You damn germaphobic, whimsical fool.
